    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create a Python script that uses a concrete external provider to decrypt a ciphertext payload with a managed key. I will choose AWS KMS (Key Management Service) as the provider because it is a widely used and well-documented service for key management and encryption/decryption operations. The script will import the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, and use it to interact with AWS KMS. The provider will be identifiable in the code through the import of boto3 and the use of AWS KMS-specific methods. </thinking>\n",
